{"name":"Be Mine","hex":"#f4e3e7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Pronoun","definitions":["That or those belonging to me.\nUsed predicatively.","Used predicatively."]},{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["My; belonging to me.\n\nUsed attributively after the noun it modifies.\n\nUsed attributively before a vowel.","Used attributively after the noun it modifies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Be Mine (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Be Mine is a novel by Richard Ford published in 2023. It is Ford's fifth book to feature Frank Bascombe as the narrator and protagonist."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Book_Cover_Be_Mine_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Be_Mine_(novel)"},{"title":"Laura Kasischke","blocks":[{"text":"Laura Kasischke is an American fiction writer and poet. She is best known for writing the novels Suspicious River, The Life Before Her Eyes and White Bird in a Blizzard, all of which have been adapted to film."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Laura_Kasischke_2011_NBCC_Awards_2012_Shankbone.JPG/330px-Laura_Kasischke_2011_NBCC_Awards_2012_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Kasischke"},{"title":"Be Mine (Infinite song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Be Mine\" is a song released by the South Korean boy band Infinite. The song is the title track of the group's first studio album Over the Top, released on July 21, 2011. The song is also the second Japanese single of the group. It was released on April 18, 2012 in 4 different editions."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Be_Mine_(Infinite_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c1/BeMine-regular.jpeg/250px-BeMine-regular.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikip